# MuriArc Server Docker Tester

> English | [简体中文](README_cn.md)

**Classification:** unsigned · synthetic-capable · not for production · not formal RC evidence

This bundle runs the MuriArc Server Tester from an immutable GHCR digest on `linux/amd64`. It is for a trusted local machine, LAN, or VPN only. It is not the signed Managed Compose Server bundle and must not be exposed directly to the public Internet.

- Source commit: `@@SOURCE_COMMIT@@`
- Server image: `@@SERVER_IMAGE@@`
- PostgreSQL image: `@@POSTGRES_IMAGE@@`
- Release tag: `@@RELEASE_TAG@@`

## 1. Verify the download

Verify the release asset itself using the adjacent `.sha256` file before extracting. Inside the extracted directory, copy one environment template and run the bundled verifier:

```bash
cp .env.empty.example .env   # or: cp .env.demo.example .env
# Replace every REPLACE_ value. Use a unique project name if another copy exists.
./muriarc-tester.sh verify
```

PowerShell:

```powershell
Copy-Item .env.empty.example .env   # or .env.demo.example
# Replace every REPLACE_ value.
.\muriarc-tester.ps1 verify
```

`verify` checks `CHECKSUMS.sha256`, the environment contract, Compose policy, and both digest-pinned images. It never prints the configured passwords.

## 2. Initialize exactly once

Choose one mode for brand-new volumes:

```bash
./muriarc-tester.sh init-empty  # empty database, recommended default
./muriarc-tester.sh init-demo   # immutable synthetic standard-v1 data
```

Both commands refuse an existing PostgreSQL or Server-data volume. Empty initialization enables preview bootstrap only for the first proven-empty start, then restarts with bootstrap disabled. Demo initialization seeds and verifies standard-v1 before the Server starts. A failure preserves the containers and volumes for diagnosis; do not clear the database or patch SQL.

The demo uses fixed synthetic Lab/User UUIDs. You still provide the Environment Root email, display name, and password. The configured Root becomes LabAdmin and can view the synthetic projects and animals.

## 3. Operate

```bash
./muriarc-tester.sh status
./muriarc-tester.sh logs
./muriarc-tester.sh down   # always preserves volumes
./muriarc-tester.sh up
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:8787` unless you changed the loopback port. PostgreSQL has no host port. No `destroy` command is provided.

## Security boundary

- Keep `.env` private and out of Git, chat, issues, and backups that are not encrypted.
- Generate different, URL-safe PostgreSQL and Root passwords. Do not reuse a personal password.
- Each Server user configures their own AI Provider and API Key in the UI. Never put Provider keys in `.env`.
- `MURIARC_SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=false` is only for direct loopback HTTP. Use a trusted private reverse proxy with HTTPS and set it to `true` for LAN/VPN access.
- Back up PostgreSQL, `server_data`, `.env`, generation metadata, attachments, and the generated AI Master Key as one recovery set.
- Real research data, Internet exposure, HA, unattended upgrade, and production restore require the signed formal Server delivery and its full acceptance process.

See the [English configuration guide](https://github.com/jarxunlai/MuriArc/blob/@@SOURCE_COMMIT@@/docs/CONFIGURATION.md) for the complete variable table and troubleshooting steps.
